      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 3}{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{13}⟨0,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\frac{4}{13},\\frac{6}{13}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
